step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple best_single strategy with ETS, since ETS is seasonality champion and top RMSE overall.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ETS"}

Thought: Test a robust median over pool3 to see if it beats the best single ETS.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool3","rationale":"robust median on moderately consistent pool"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool3 using inverse_error weights to see if weighting improves over median and best_single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["ARIMA","ETS","THETA","DWT_rf","FT_rf","DWT_catboost"],"weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median on the larger pool2 to see if expanding the pool improves over current weighted result.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a robust median on the smallest stable pool (pool1) to see if fewer models improve robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1","rationale":"median on highly correlated but stable subset"}

Thought: Test a simple mean over pool4 to see if pooling fewer models improves the score.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool3 using inverse_error weights to see if it improves over the current best mean pool4.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool3","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean over the robust pool4 to see if trimming improves over mean and weighted results.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool4","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a robust median over the most diverse pool4 to see if median can beat weighted or mean in this trend‑dominated series.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Try a weighted combination using inverse_error weights on the robust pool4 to see if weighting improves over median/mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool4","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a DTW barycenter on the diverse pool4 to see if it beats the weighted mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool4","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on pool3 to see if trimming improves over mean/weighted on that pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool3","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a DTW barycenter on the smaller, more stable pool1 to see if a focused DTW improves over weighted/trimmed results.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a DTW barycenter on the moderately sized pool2 to see if it can beat the weighted mean on pool4.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool2","dba_max_iter":30}

